    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Stack is delighted to present this substantial and beautifully proportioned 4-bedroom, 3-bathroom detached residence to the market. Set on a generous 0.91-acre (0.37 ha) landscaped site, this impressive property perfectly balances rural tranquility with exceptional commuter convenience.\nSituated just off the main N69 route, the property offers easy access to nearby Kilflynn Village (5 mins), Listowel (10 mins) and Tralee (15 mins).\nThe bright, versatile layout is designed for modern family living and working from home. Ground Floor accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, open-plan living/dining room, kitchen, utility room, two bedrooms (master with ensuite shower room and walk in wardrobe) and a family bathroom. On the first floor there is two additional double bedrooms, office/study, storeroom, and shower room. The exterior is a standout feature - ideal for families, hobbyists, or trade professionals with a large garage/workshop (79 sqm) and garden shed (14 sq m) and a tarmacadam driveway framed by mature trees, hedging, and lawns.\nCombining generous living spaces, mature grounds, and a highly convenient location, this property is certain to appeal to a wide range of purchasers. Viewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 3.90m x 1.66m\nwith wooden flooring\n\nHallway - 3.95m x 2.34m\nwith carpet flooring, stairs to 1st floor & 2 windows\n\nLiving / Dining Room - 7.25m x 3.94m\nwith solid fuel stove (with back boiler), solid wood flooring, 4 windows (dual aspect) and sliding patio doors to rear garden\n\nKitchen - 5.05m x 3.30m\nfitted kitchen with wall & floor tiles, solid fuel stove & 2 windows. This rooms opens into the living/dining room.\n\nUtility Room - 2.41m x 1.75m\nwith fitted units, washing machine, floor tiles and half glazed door to rear.\n\nAiring Cupboard - 2.95m x 1.20m\nwalk in with tiled flooring.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 8.91m x 3.94m\nDouble with carpet flooring & 3 windows (dual aspect)\n\nEnsuite - 3.92m x 1.01m\nTriton electric shower, mosaic style wall & floor tiles, whb, w/c & window\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.67m x 1.50m\nshelved with carpet flooring\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.08m x 2.71m\nDouble with carpet flooring & 2 windows\n\nFamily Bathroom - 3.34m x 2.83m\nSpacious & modern glass shower enclosure (1.78m x 0.83m) with rainfall power shower, wall & floor tiles, whb, w/c & window\n\n1st floor corridor - 988m x 1.49m\nwith carpet flooring & Velux\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.14m x 3.95m\nDouble with carpet flooring & Velux\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.13m x 3.94m\nDouble with carpet flooring & Velux\n\nShower Room - 2.46m x 2.21m\nwith Triton T80i shower, wall & floor tiles, whb, w/c & Velux\n\nStudy/Office - 3.52m x 2.46m\nwith carpet flooring & Velux\n\nStore - 2.77m x 1.59m\naccess to heating controls, wooden flooring\n\nOutbuildings - \n\n\nGarage/Workshop/Store - 79 sq m\n\n\nGarden Shed - 14 sqm\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>4 bedroom, 3 bathroom detached property set on a mature landscaped 0.91 acre site </li><li>Central location - just five minutes from the village of Kilflynn</li><li>10 mins to the heritage town of Listowel </li><li>15 mins to the county town of Tralee</li><li>Excellent range of outbuildings (79 sq m & 14 sq m) - ideal storage, workshop, hobby or DIY space.</li><li>Oil-fired central heating, two solid-fuel stoves (one with back boiler), </li><li>Double-glazed uPVC windows throughout </li><li>On-site septic tank.</li><li>Fibre broadband available </li><li></li><li></li><li>Killarney - 40 mins</ul>"
      },
